                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "soup",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "663fda68-03d0-3224-b411-7f02ce1afc01",
                                        "entry_id": "7c14d2b8-5ac3-3b7f-9cf3-fe1578f399cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To feed: to provide with soup or a meal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0018f39f-91d7-449e-8fc0-b30570087bb4",
                                                "sense_id": "663fda68-03d0-3224-b411-7f02ce1afc01",
                                                "text": "I'm blessed if I've heard about any thing but kangaroo-tail soup all the while I was at Launceston. They souped me there night and day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8247ca3b-7cbf-4ab2-b559-61036dd205fb",
                                                "sense_id": "663fda68-03d0-3224-b411-7f02ce1afc01",
                                                "text": "Now laughing together thaws our human ice; long before Swindon it was a talking match, —at Swindon who so devoted as Captain Dolignan,—he handed them out—he souped them,—he tough-chickened them,—he brandied and cochinealed one, and he brandied and burnt-sugared the other;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "991edb13-e26f-462d-8670-726882061f04",
                                                "sense_id": "663fda68-03d0-3224-b411-7f02ce1afc01",
                                                "text": "\"I was so mad, I let him wait half an hour to-night before I souped him.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf050d37-eeaa-4906-8bf1-7e94bf8eca73",
                                                "sense_id": "663fda68-03d0-3224-b411-7f02ce1afc01",
                                                "text": "She cooked huge stock pots and souped her dogs once a day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1860e9c9-e0d4-4dc3-be92-2e6f1fb70f13",
                                                "sense_id": "663fda68-03d0-3224-b411-7f02ce1afc01",
                                                "text": "I souped the dogs, and went in for a bite. I ended up going back out and making my pups a full meal, then went back in and pigged out myself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75427ce3-60a6-38b7-b6bc-cdc17ec751f4",
                                        "entry_id": "7c14d2b8-5ac3-3b7f-9cf3-fe1578f399cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To develop (film) in a (chemical) developing solution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "785c90aa-90e5-4067-8de8-b87f0d67bdc0",
                                                "sense_id": "75427ce3-60a6-38b7-b6bc-cdc17ec751f4",
                                                "text": "That girl Vivienne, by the way, once worked as a secretary in the workshop of The Rotarian, began \"souping\" her own snapshots at home, went from there to top rank as a New York color photographer specializing in small children […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff5db4ed-ede8-4ba4-ba01-f43ded314d3f",
                                                "sense_id": "75427ce3-60a6-38b7-b6bc-cdc17ec751f4",
                                                "text": "\"Then perhaps it won't surprise you to learn Annie's taking over the Sunday social column,\" Roz said. \"You photo-guys'll be souping her film.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "871f566c-788c-4d19-9750-fcdfb60e1d2a",
                                                "sense_id": "75427ce3-60a6-38b7-b6bc-cdc17ec751f4",
                                                "text": "And her camera position had been completely out of his sight. Satisfied that she'd gotten everything she'd needed - much more, in fact - she went back inside and got to work. Jill had souped her first photographs while she'd been on […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "104d2073-e4b2-4828-ae6c-c94af0491d08",
                                                "sense_id": "75427ce3-60a6-38b7-b6bc-cdc17ec751f4",
                                                "text": "By 6 pm Beau and I are back at the paper, souping the film, when Woody rushes into the room."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                        "entry_id": "7c14d2b8-5ac3-3b7f-9cf3-fe1578f399cf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To proselytize by feeding the impoverished as long as they listen to one's preaching."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9202943-6d41-422c-9c76-ce0de462f24d",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                                "text": "Was the priest who denounced those books of the National Board as \"souping books\" the patron of a national school?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a4d4799-e660-4b72-b236-4936a48c11ee",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                                "text": "\"Souping\" in Peterstown came to an end, and Una had enough to do with her full school and ignorant scholars to deaden the sting of her grief for the time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8400bb16-8db6-42c4-8d71-e76af44db76e",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                                "text": "It was suggested that the briefs should be distributed generally; but they could not be spread as they were at Manchester, Liverpool, and Leeds, where briefs where \"souped\" out."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6438579-94a0-4fb8-a871-a1087a611dcb",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                                "text": "Yes, and it was all done in pure charity, no souping swaddling mixture whatever. The Fitz-Ffoulkes had none of that about them ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b64890fc-590e-45e3-ae45-b86fdad3709c",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                                "text": "Before long we passed a Scripture-reader (such the driver said he was), reading a book as a priest does his breviary. I though him not out of place; for anything madder than the whole system of \"souping\" it is hard to imagine. In Kerry you see signs of it here and there, as you do in Connemara."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "433ed979-e807-4b9f-afce-e77aa9e2e3a4",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ad5fe3-c84c-3de3-9edb-a35aeea08b6c",
                                                "text": "I ask, Sir, what right has the hon. Member to call any Protestant minister a souping parson?."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "soup",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
